// expect: 7
// SYNTAX §«Records»: the record literal reads a contextual keyword as a
// field NAME (`{own: …}`), so field ACCESS reads it the same way. Measured
// 2026-09-25: `r.own` parsed to a field named "" — the parser's fallback
// for a token that is not an identifier — and surfaced as a record type
// mismatch against a field with no name, `{ : t } vs { own: Int }`.
// Exit 7 is the field read back.
fn owned(r) = r.own

fn main() = owned({own: 7})
